)","kind":"symbol","fragments":[{"text":"func","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"girth","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"() -> ","kind":"text"},{"preciseIdentifier":"s:Si","text":"Int","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":"?","kind":"text"}],"role":"symbol","abstract":[{"type":"text","text":"The length of a shortest cycle, in edges: 1 when there is a self-loop, 2 when there is a"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"pair of parallel edges; "},{"type":"codeVoice","code":"nil"},{"type":"text","text":" when the graph is acyclic."}],"url":"\/documentation\/cycles\/graphprotocols\/graph\/girth()","identifier":"doc:\/\/Cycles\/documentation\/Cycles\/GraphProtocols\/Graph\/girth()"}}}